## Codex Review (GPT-5.5)
Reviewed the full PR branch against freshly fetched `upstream/master`; dominant type is `bug-fix` with secondary `tests`, `a11y`, and bundle-size impact. The hover-specific fix is well covered, but keyboard focus and delayed-open timing still leave branch-relevant regressions.

### 1. Bugs / Issues

#### 1. 🔴 Inner trigger focus can still open the outer tooltip (blocking)

`packages/react/src/tooltip/trigger/TooltipTrigger.tsx`

```tsx
const focusProps = useFocus(floatingRootContext, { enabled: !disabled }).reference;

// ...

props: [
  hoverProps,
  focusProps,
  rootTriggerProps,
  {
    onMouseOver(event: React.MouseEvent) {
      handleNestedTriggerHover(event.nativeEvent);
    },
```

The nested-trigger guard only covers hover. React `onFocus` bubbles, so focusing an enabled inner `Tooltip.Trigger` inside an outer trigger can run both focus handlers and open both ancestor and inner tooltips for keyboard users.

**Fix:** add the nested-trigger veto to focus opens as well, either through a `useFocus` `shouldOpen` guard or an internal `onFocus` handler that calls `event.preventBaseUIHandler()` when the focus target is an enabled descendant tooltip trigger. Add a regression test for focusing the uncontrolled inner trigger.

#### 2. 🟡 A stale parent hover timer can open too early after returning from the nested trigger (non-blocking)

`packages/react/src/floating-ui-react/hooks/useHoverReferenceInteraction.ts`

```ts
instance.openChangeTimeout.start(openDelay, () => {
  if (shouldOpen && checkShouldOpen()) {
    store.setOpen(true, createChangeEventDetails(REASONS.triggerHover, event, triggerNode));
  }
});
```

If the pointer starts over the outer area, moves onto the inner trigger before the outer delay expires, then moves back to the parent area before the original timer fires, `shouldOpen()` becomes true again and the old timer can open the parent earlier than a fresh parent-area delay.

**Fix:** cancel or invalidate pending hover/rest opens when nested hover starts, or tie delayed callbacks to an epoch. Add a test for outer hover -> half delay -> inner hover -> parent-area return, asserting the parent waits a full new delay.

#### 3. 🟡 Two regression tests do not prove the edge cases their names claim (non-blocking)

`packages/react/src/tooltip/root/TooltipRoot.test.tsx`

```tsx
// Disabled nested trigger case only hovers the outer trigger.
const outerTrigger = screen.getByTestId('outer-trigger');

fireEvent.pointerDown(outerTrigger, { pointerType: 'mouse' });
fireEvent.pointerEnter(outerTrigger, { clientX: 10, clientY: 10 });
```

The disabled nested-trigger test never hovers the disabled inner trigger, so it would pass even if disabled nested triggers were still treated as enabled.

```tsx
const innerShadowTarget = document.createElement('span');
innerShadowRoot.appendChild(innerShadowTarget);

innerShadowRoot.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('mouseover', { bubbles: true, composed: true }));
```

The shadow-root test dispatches from the `ShadowRoot`, not `innerShadowTarget`, so it does not really prove traversal from an element inside the shadow tree back to the host trigger.

**Fix:** hover the disabled inner trigger in the disabled case, and dispatch the composed shadow event from `innerShadowTarget`.

### Performance Considerations

I ran `pnpm size:snapshot` on the PR head and on the PR merge-base (`53c3d1e`) to isolate the branch delta.

| Entry | Parsed Δ | Gzip Δ |
|---|---:|---:|
| `@base-ui/react/tooltip` | +1,197 B | +449 B |
| `@base-ui/react` | +1,192 B | +481 B |
| `@base-ui/react/internals/shadowDom` | +220 B | +78 B |
| Shared hover users such as `menu`, `popover`, `preview-card` | +73 B each | +32-40 B each |

Best bundle-size reductions to try:

1. Only mark enabled triggers with `data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger`, then simplify the selector to `[data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger]`.
2. Replace the shared exported `closest()` helper with a tooltip-local composed-path/host scan that checks the marker directly; this should remove the `shadowDom` entrypoint growth and the extra re-export cost.
3. Compute `event.composedPath()` once in `TooltipTrigger` and drop the separate `getTarget` import for this path.

### Test Coverage Assessment

`pnpm test:jsdom TooltipRoot --no-watch` passed on the PR head. Coverage is broad for pointer hover, detached handles, disabled triggers, shadow DOM, and zero-delay providers, but it needs the focus regression and stale-delay regression above before this is safe to merge.

### Recommendation

Request changes 🔴

The pointer-hover fix is directionally solid, but the keyboard focus path can still produce nested ancestor tooltips, which is an accessibility regression. I’d also address the stale timer before merge because it preserves the old flicker/early-open class of bug in a fast pointer path.
